  'recon.pin.idle': '★Every question on this page is really "what did that change". Press "Pin this run" to keep the current result on the figures, change something, run again, and read the two side by side.',
  'recon.basis.raw.short': 'raw channels',
  'recon.preset': 'Analysis presets',
  'recon.preset.what': '★This column carries some forty knobs and any one question needs five or six of them. A preset is not a shortcut past understanding: it <strong>states what it assumes</strong> in the same breath as applying it. Pressing one changes settings and <strong>does not run</strong> — whether to compute stays your decision.',
  'recon.preset.mag': 'Magnetics only',
  'recon.preset.kin': 'Kinetic',
  'recon.preset.ramp': 'Current ramp',
  'recon.preset.twin': 'Twin self-check',
  'recon.preset.applied': 'Applied the "{what}" preset — settings changed, <strong>nothing computed yet</strong>.',
  'recon.preset.note.mag': '<strong>Magnetics only</strong>: flux loops plus the I<sub>p</sub> equality constraint, with pressure, density, probes, point diagnostics and the vessel all off. ★This is the <strong>quality baseline</strong>: every other tier should be compared against it, and every extra constraint should be able to say what it bought.',
  'recon.preset.note.kin': '<strong>Kinetic</strong>: pressure rows (9 points, relative weight 0.2) and the density channel, with the density fitted to the interferometer. ★The pressure comes from the deck\'s delivered profile or from the profile-fit bar — it is an input that is <strong>believed</strong>, not a product of this fit.',
  'recon.preset.note.ramp': '<strong>Current ramp</strong>: vessel eddy currents on (truncated SVD, rcond 0.05) with the probes, pressure off — a ramp has no trustworthy pressure profile and the vessel carries induced current. ★The identifiability threshold still applies: when it cannot be determined the page refuses rather than answering. ★<strong>It does not converge on the bundled shot</strong> (measured: singular normal equations at outer iteration 137), and that is not a wrong setting: with flux loops alone the vessel eddy currents are not identifiable in the first place (T-A6 — 5.6 % left after projecting the vessel modes out, below the fit\'s own model error). This preset is for a <strong>live ramp-phase slice</strong>, where the vessel really does carry induced current; the slice this repository ships is a flat-top one.',
  'recon.preset.note.twin': '<strong>Twin self-check</strong>: switch to the synthetic twin (truth known), turn on probes, interferometer and Faraday with synthesised readings, Faraday weight at the 0.25 the sweep found. ★This tier judges the method, not this machine\'s shot.',
  'recon.source': 'Data source',
