  'recon.tab.real.title': 'This device carries no measured data',
  'recon.basis.pick': 'Channel basis',
  'recon.basis.delivered': '★<strong>Delivered reconstruction values</strong>: the {loops} flux loops carry what another code concluded each channel should read ({prov}). This is the page default and the basis the shipped fit settings were tuned against; ★probes need a matching channel file to be <strong>imported</strong> — the deck\'s probes are raw readings and do not belong to this basis.',
  'recon.basis.raw': '★<strong>Raw est2 readings</strong>: the {loops} flux loops carry the measured <strong>total</strong> flux (the page removes the coils\' share with the response it fits against), and the {probes} probes and {chords} POINT chords are raw as well. ★One basis at a time: feeding delivered and raw values to one fit asks a single solution to satisfy two different statements about the same shot. ★<strong>What this basis costs on the bundled shot is measurable</strong>: at the loops the coil share is <strong>3.03×</strong> the plasma signal (rms 0.349 vs 0.115 Wb/rad), and after this page subtracts it the result sits <strong>5.1 %</strong> away from the delivered channel values (up to 12.8 % on one channel, 16 positive and 14 negative — a <strong>shape</strong>, not an offset a fit could absorb). Held exact, that 5 % goes into the residual and the fit stands: residual 5.15e-5, weighted χ² 8.60e-4 (the delivered basis reaches 1.98e-8 / 4.55e-4). ★But this shot has <strong>no spare information for a second unknown</strong> — set the coils free and the normal equations go singular at outer iteration 78; turn the vessel eddies on and they go at 137.',
