  'recon.pdecomp.what': '★★<strong>What a kinetic reconstruction is actually constrained by</strong>: the equilibrium sees the <strong>total</strong> pressure (thermal + fast ions + rotation), while Thomson/CXRS measure the thermal part and the bootstrap current is driven by the <strong>thermal</strong> gradient. Handing a thermal profile over as though it were the total is the standard way a beam-heated discharge comes out with the wrong p′, and the fit cannot notice. ★Neither term is invented here: an imported fast-ion profile is used when there is one, and the fraction below is a <strong>shape you set</strong> (zero by default, and its provenance travels with every file); rotation pressure needs ω(ψ) and a mass density, for which this page has no channel, so it is <strong>only ever imported</strong>.',
