  'recon.vessel': 'Vessel eddy currents',
  'recon.vessel.what': 'Every fit on this page treats the external field as <strong>exactly known</strong>: the coil currents are given, the vacuum flux follows, and whatever the loops see beyond that is the plasma. That holds at flat-top; during a <strong>current ramp, a vertical excursion or a disruption precursor</strong> it does not — the vessel carries induced currents of its own, and a fit with nowhere to put them puts them in p′ and FF′. The deck describes the vessel (90 elements on EAST, in three groups), so those currents can be an unknown instead of an error. ★What is fitted is <strong>one total current per group</strong>, distributed inside a group by element conductance (area / resistivity, i.e. a uniform loop voltage across the group) — that is a <strong>model</strong>: a group whose current is not distributed that way is not in this family, and the residual will say so.',
