  'recon.coilfit': 'Coil currents in the fit',
  'recon.coilfit.what': '★<strong>T-A5</strong>: the solver used to treat the coil currents as <strong>exactly known</strong> — they appeared only on the right-hand side, as the vacuum field and as the share subtracted from every channel reading. On this shot the raw Rogowski currents differ from the delivered reconstruction\'s own fitted values by <strong>2–9 %</strong> channel to channel, and all nine slices failed. With this on, the coil currents join the fitted parameters, each carrying a sigma prior — which is what EFIT itself does.',
  'recon.coilfit.on': 'Treat the coil currents as observations carrying sigma',
  'recon.adv.coilfit': 'Advanced: the two sigmas',
  'recon.coilsig': 'Coil current relative sigma',
  'recon.loopsig': 'Flux-loop sigma / max|psi|',
  'recon.coilfit.note': '★<strong>This switch asks for TWO sigmas, not one.</strong> A weighted least squares is a posterior only when <code>w = 1/sigma</code>, and every deck here ships flux-loop weights that are a <strong>0/1 mask</strong> — which asserts sigma_loop = 1 Wb/rad. Against a coil prior of a few per cent that assertion says the loops are worthless and the fit <strong>does not move</strong>: measured on #137985 @ 4 s, a 20 % coil prior shifted the currents by 3e-4 of themselves and li(3) fell only 21.30 to 18.06. Fitting coil currents therefore obliges you to say how well the loops are measured. Now: coil sigma = {c} x |I_channel| (a channel reading zero is <strong>held</strong>), loop sigma = {l} x max|psi_plasma|.',
  'recon.coilfit.done': 'Coil fit: {n} channels free, largest excursion {pull} sigma (the cap is {cap} sigma).',
  'recon.reject.coil': 'The coil currents were moved too far: the largest excursion is {pull} sigma against a cap of {cap}. The fit bought its residual by ceasing to believe the calibration it was handed, and that is not a reconstruction of the shot that ran.',
  'ser.coilsrc.slice.fit': '★The coil currents are <strong>fitted too</strong> (the switch in the reconstruction bar is on): each slice\'s raw Rogowski currents stop being an equality input and become the centre of a prior, one sigma per channel. Measured at the shipped sigmas: <strong>eight</strong> of the nine slices converge, li(3) 1.18–1.85, coil excursions 0.98–1.49 sigma; t = 4 s still does not solve (the plasma mask collapses mid-iteration). With the switch off, none of the nine lands in li(3) in [0.5, 3].',
