  'recon.mc.absent': '★What this page cannot do is said out loud too. <strong>Now readable backwards</strong>: the magnetic probes (import their readings, or let the twin synthesise them) and the POINT interferometer and polarimeter (likewise) — they both predict and constrain. <strong>Still out of reach</strong>: (1) Thomson n<sub>e</sub>/T<sub>e</sub> are not in the deck, so the profile-fit bar can only take imported points or a resampling of the deck\'s delivered profile; (2) <strong>the geometry of MSE and of an SXR tomography camera is in none of the shipped device decks</strong> — the kernel carries the tomography basis and its response rows, so what is missing is device DATA, not wiring; (3) the self-consistency loop between the bootstrap and the fitted current is now <strong>closed</strong> (T-A9 landed the per-surface ⟨j·B⟩↔⟨j_φ⟩ conversion and the neoclassical conductivity σ<sub>neo</sub>), but the posterior does <strong>not</strong> sample the outer loop — these error bars are about the four sources listed, not about the self-consistent iteration.',
