  "b.lim_source": "★<strong>These limits are yours, not the machine’s.</strong> Real supply ratings would come from the device descriptor, and neither descriptor here carries a set that has been cross-checked: two upstream sources disagree on the <strong>turn counts</strong> of the PF7/PF9-type elements, and a limit is derived by dividing by turns — so a limit from the wrong turn count attaches <strong>silently to the wrong channel</strong>, and the page would say “blocked by PF3” while the coil actually saturating is another one. So this page asks rather than invents. Each channel is editable; moving the uniform slider above means “all of them” and clears the per-channel edits.",
  "b.verdict.nocon": "★<strong>Not converged, so these currents are not a design</strong> — the bounded solve reached its iteration cap and this is the last step of a descent. The figure and the table show that step; do not read it as an optimum. Loosen the per-channel limits, raise the regularisation, or ask for a weaker |B|, and run again.",
  "b.verdict.nolimit": "No current limit applied. |B|<sub>max</sub> = {b} mT (criterion {tol} mT) — this tier answers “how good can it get with unlimited current”, not “can this machine do it”.",
  "b.verdict.ok": "<strong>Feasible</strong>: |B|<sub>max</sub> = {b} mT meets the criterion and no channel is at its bound — the limits are not what constrains this design.",
  "b.verdict.ok_bind": "<strong>Feasible, but hard against the limits</strong>: |B|<sub>max</sub> = {b} mT meets the criterion, at the cost of <strong>{who}</strong> sitting at the bound. Push the parameters a little further and that is what stops you.",
  "b.verdict.blocked": "<strong>Infeasible: blocked by the current limit on {who}.</strong> |B|<sub>max</sub> = {b} mT against a criterion of {tol} mT. Either raise those channels’ limits or move the null to where they can reach it — <strong>knowing who blocked it is what gives you a second move</strong>.",
  "b.verdict.short": "<strong>Infeasible, but not by the limits</strong>: |B|<sub>max</sub> = {b} mT exceeds the {tol} mT criterion while no channel is at its bound. This coil set simply cannot make a null that weak at this place; raising the limits will not help.",
