  // ===== T-A9: the bootstrap / ohmic / fitted-current closure (one block) =====
  'recon.closure': 'Bootstrap · ohmic · fitted current',
  'recon.closure.what': 'The fit gives ⟨j<sub>φ</sub>⟩; the analytic bootstrap family gives ⟨j·B⟩ — <strong>two different quantities</strong>, which is why they could not be subtracted. This kernel batch added the per-surface conversion (the exact Grad-Shafranov identity) and the neoclassical conductivity σ<sub>neo</sub>, so three curves now live in one measure, ⟨j·B⟩/B₀, and <strong>add up</strong>: j<sub>tot</sub> = j<sub>bs</sub> + j<sub>ohm</sub>. With the outer loop on, the bootstrap current goes onto the kernel\'s <strong>prescribed-current channel</strong>, the magnetics fit only the remainder, and the rounds run until the bootstrap fraction stops moving.',
