  'recon.closure.row.identity': 'Conversion identity residual (relative)',
  'recon.closure.row.sigma': 'σ<sub>neo</sub> coefficients',
  'recon.closure.row.f33': 'Trapping factor F₃₃, range',
  'recon.closure.row.rounds': 'Outer rounds',
  'recon.closure.row.spread': 'Bootstrap fraction, spread across rounds',
  'recon.closure.row.hist': 'Bootstrap fraction, round by round',
  'recon.closure.cap': '★The three curves are in {unit}. What converts the fitted ⟨j<sub>φ</sub>⟩ into the parallel measure is the kernel entry <code>fylite_rs_jparb_jphi</code>; the p′ term in that conversion is the <strong>diamagnetic</strong> current, which belongs to the total and to neither channel — so it is the fit that gets converted, not the parts. The loop voltage implied on axis by ⟨j<sub>ohm</sub>·B⟩ = σ<sub>neo</sub>⟨E·B⟩ is {vloop} V; that it is <strong>not the same on every surface</strong> is precisely the statement that a magnetics-only current profile is not the neoclassical ohmic one.',
  'recon.ser.jtot': 'j_tot (fit, converted)',
  'recon.ser.johm': 'j_ohm = j_tot − j_bs',
  'recon.ser.jbs2': 'j_bs (Redl-2021)',
  'recon.ser.sigsp': 'σ_Spitzer (Sauter form)',
  'recon.ser.signeo': 'σ_neo (with trapping)',
  'recon.axis.jsplit': '⟨j·B⟩/B₀ [MA/m²]',
  'recon.axis.sigma': 'σ∥ [MS/m]',
  'recon.jsplit_cap': 'Three <strong>addable</strong> curves in one measure, ⟨j·B⟩/B₀: the fitted total, the ohmic remainder and the bootstrap. ★The fitted one is assembled from that fit\'s own p′ and FF′ through ⟨B²⟩ and then compared, surface by surface, with the kernel\'s conversion; the identity residual is in the table above.',
  'recon.signeo_cap': 'Parallel conductivity: Sauter\'s Spitzer form (dashed) and σ<sub>neo</sub> with the trapped-particle correction (solid). ★Their ratio F₃₃ is where the <strong>shape</strong> of the ohmic current comes from — trapping removes more than a third of it between the axis and mid-radius, and the <code>fylite_rs_spitzer_eta</code> tier cannot state that shape at all (since v111 it carries the parallel branch 0.51 η<sub>⊥</sub>, 0.2 % from this form at Z=1 — before T-A18 it carried the NRL perpendicular coefficient, off by 1/0.51).',

